disableSchemaApply|disableSchemaApply|false|false|Set to disable schema from being applied.
disableRuntimeResult|disableRuntimeResult|false|false|Set to disable writing detailed CSV file during query execution. Those will eventually get written at the end of query execution.
z|zookeeper|true|false|HBase Zookeeper address for connection. Default: localhost
q|query|false|false|Executes multi-threaded query sets
listFiles|listFiles|false|false|List available resource files
mt|multi-tenant|false|false|Multi tenanted workloads based on load profiles.
l|load|false|false|Pre-loads data according to specified configuration values.
scenarioFile|scenarioFile|true|false|Regex or file name for the Test Scenario configuration .xml file to use.
scenarioName|scenarioName|true|false|Regex or scenario name from the Test Scenario configuration .xml file to use.
drop|drop|true|false|Regex drop all tables with schema name as PHERF. \nExample drop Event tables: -drop .*(EVENT).* Drop all: -drop .* or -drop all
schemaFile|schemaFile|true|false|Regex or file name for the Test phoenix table schema .sql to use.
m|monitor|false|false|Launch the stats profilers
monitorFrequency|monitorFrequency|true|false|Override for frequency in Ms for which monitor should log stats. \n See pherf.default.monitorFrequency in pherf.properties
rowCountOverride|rowCountOverride|true|false|Row count override to use instead of one specified in scenario.
hint|hint|true|false|Executes all queries with specified hint. Example SMALL
log_per_nrows|log_per_nrows|true|false|Default value to display log line after every 'N' row load
diff|diff|false|false|Run pherf in verification mode and diff with exported results
export|export|false|false|Exports query results to CSV files in CSV_EXPORT directory
writerThreadSize|writerThreadSize|true|false|Override the default number of writer threads. See pherf.default.dataloader.threadpool in Pherf.properties.
h|help|false|false|Get help on using this utility.
d|debug|false|false|Put tool in debug mode
stats|stats|false|false|Update Phoenix Statistics after data is loaded with -l argument
label|label|true|false|Label a run. Result file name will be suffixed with specified label
compare|compare|true|false|Specify labeled run(s) to compare
useAverageCompareType|useAverageCompareType|false|false|Compare results with Average query time instead of default is Minimum query time.
t|thin|false|false|Use the Phoenix Thin Driver
s|server|true|false|The URL for the Phoenix QueryServer
b|batchApi|false|false|Use JDBC Batch API for writes
